BT /F2 10.5 Tf 0.08 0.29 0.29 rg 48 416.9999999999995 Td (Question: Why use both a public Supabase client and an admin client?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.2 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.20 rg 48 402.4999999999995 Td (Answer: The public client is appropriate for user-authenticated Auth operations. The) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.2 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.20 rg 48 389.2999999999995 Td (admin/service client is backend-only and lets requireAuth reload profiles and controllers) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.2 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.20 rg 48 376.0999999999995 Td (perform controlled server operations. Keeping the secret out of the browser limits exposure.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.5 Tf 0.08 0.29 0.29 rg 48 353.8999999999995 Td (Question: Why is the profile reloaded after validating a token?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.2 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.20 rg 48 339.3999999999995 Td (Answer: A JWT alone may contain stale role or active-state assumptions. requireAuth queries) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.2 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.20 rg 48 326.19999999999953 Td (profiles and checks is_active, so authorization uses current database state.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.5 Tf 0.08 0.29 0.29 rg 48 303.99999999999955 Td (Question: Why are booking slots calculated in a service?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.2 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.20 rg 48 289.49999999999955 Td (Answer: Slot generation combines hours, appointments, time-off, UTC dates, durations, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.2 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.20 rg 48 276.29999999999956 Td (overlaps. Keeping it in availabilityService makes the rule reusable and directly testable.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.5 Tf 0.08 0.29 0.29 rg 48 254.09999999999957 Td (Question: How is a double booking prevented?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.2 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.20 rg 48 239.59999999999957 Td (Answer: The controller computes eligibility and handles the database conflict/race path; tests) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.2 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.20 rg 48 226.39999999999958 Td (explicitly cover a slot lost to a concurrent booking and return a clear 409 response.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.5 Tf 0.08 0.29 0.29 rg 48 204.1999999999996 Td (Question: Why does the frontend have one folder per assessment region?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.2 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.20 rg 48 189.6999999999996 Td (Answer: Regions have different fields and clinical tests. Separate data/config/sections) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.2 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.20 rg 48 176.4999999999996 Td (prevent a single permissive form from accepting invalid region vocabulary while shared) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.2 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.20 rg 48 163.2999999999996 Td (controls keep the UI consistent.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.5 Tf 0.08 0.29 0.29 rg 48 141.09999999999962 Td (Question: Why use PATCH for drafts?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.2 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.20 rg 48 126.59999999999962 Td (Answer: PATCH represents partial modification. Assessment pages autosave drafts and update) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.2 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.20 rg 48 113.39999999999962 Td (only the current aggregate without pretending to replace an unrelated resource.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.5 Tf 0.08 0.29 0.29 rg 48 91.19999999999962 Td (Question: How are patients prevented from seeing other patients?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.2 Tf 0.12 0.18 0.20 rg 48 76.69999999999962 Td (Answer: Backend ownership checks, role middleware, clinician assignment/appointment checks,) Tj ET
